{
	"_meta": {
		"schema": "db-ux/example/v1",
		"pageType": "contentpage",
		"origin": "guideline-authored",
		"purpose": "Canonical reference composition for a content page, authored to demonstrate the DB UX layout guidelines with the R=lg spacing model. Structure: hero (centered heading + optional subline + Brand/Filled group) → media-text rows (alternating) → image-teaser feature grid → card-teaser grid → wide highlight card → closing CTA. DENSITY/STYLE REFERENCE ONLY — compose real pages by SELECTING sections via sections.json and drawing patterns from block-patterns.json / blocks.json, not by copying this skeleton.",
		"spacingModel": "R = lg. Elements in a block, a VERTICAL Visual→content, card padding and section title↔description = lg; content blocks to each other (horizontal AND vertical) = xl; section header → content = 2xl. EXCEPTION: a HORIZONTAL Visual→text (media-text row's 50-50 grid) = xl. A vertical image-teaser is a single flat lg block (image stacked as a normal element).",
		"colorModel": "emphasis-100 (color.text.strong) is the default for headings AND body/description copy; a Topline is Small + Bold + emphasis-100; only Meta uses color.text.muted (80). See blocks.json → _meta.colorModel.",
		"conventions": "Concept Heading/Body (never raw Text). Centered contentWidth 'Medium (1024)'. Hero = centered Heading + optional subline + button group (Brand primary + optional Filled secondary); centered sections auto-center their text children. Teaser = Topline? + Heading + description + optional Tag+meta + Link, one flat block at R (lg). Feature/teaser grids use image-top teasers (flat lg) or card teasers; grid gap = xl (content blocks). Media-text rows alternate image side; 50-50 grid, gridGap xl (horizontal visual→text exception); stacked rows at xl; text column fillHeight, inner gap lg. Closing CTA = centered Heading + a single Brand Button. Zebra: canvas → surface. Section title = h2; teaser/media-text headings = h3, compact card titles = h4. Header shows app name + other pages (no 'Startseite'); meta-nav + action icons off."
	},
